notes.body:
> On UN*Xes, should the merge code try raising the file descriptor limit itself, and only do it in multiple batches if the hard limit is too low?

Sure, we can try raising the soft limit to the minimum of what we need and the hard limit.

From what I've read, on at least some versions of MacOS (Leopard and later, maybe fixed in recent version, this doesn't succeed if `rl.rlim_max > OPEN_MAX`:

```
if (getrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE, &rl) == 0) {
  rl.rlim_cur = rl.rlim_max;
  setrllimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE, &rl);
}
```

https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/System/Conceptual/ManPages_iPhoneOS/man2/setrlimit.2.html

Even in the case where `rl.rlim_max == RLIM_INFINITY` (or any other value above `OPEN_MAX`), which the system happily ignores and uses OPEN_MAX as the real, effective limit of open files:

https://www.winehq.org/pipermail/wine-devel/2022-April/214082.html

